  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1152 PM CDT TUE SEP 8 2026\n\nPersistent upper-level ridging and elevated heat will remain the\nprimary weather story throughout most of the forecast period.\nAfternoon high temperatures will generally reach the low to mid-\n90s into the weekend, with heat index values consistently topping\ntriple digits. Although conditions are expected to stay below\nofficial heat advisory thresholds, prolonged exposure outdoors\nwill continue to pose a risk of heat-related illness. By Friday,\nthe ridge should compress slightly as a deep trough and\nassociated cold front move across the Midwest. As the front loses\nupper-level support, it is forecast to stall near northern\nTennessee, bringing more organized rain chances through the\nweekend. Perhaps the best chances we have seen over the last few\nweeks. \n\nForecast confidence diminishes next week as the ridge begins to \nrebuild over the region. Model guidance varies, with some \nsolutions stronger and quicker, while others suggest a more \ngradual return and higher rain chances, though confidence remains\nlow. Ultimately, the ridge is expected to re-establish itself in \nsome capacity, pushing afternoon highs back into the low to \nmid-90s.\n\n16",
